From 2ee53efc71a003cbf6974ac2c613042545940eb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hung Fan Lin <leolin84200704@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 15:53:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [VP-17651] Match manifest to live mitigation: 30s pool
 acquire timeout, 8 replicas, 3 browsers/worker

Burst load exhausts the browser pool; with renders holding a browser
2-33s, the 10s generic-pool acquire timeout converted queue waits into
HTTP 500 (TimeoutError: ResourceRequest timed out) at ~10% of requests
during the 2026-08-06 18Z and 2026-08-07 15-16Z peaks (236 occurrences
Aug 5-10). The report viewer surfaces each as 'Failed to Download PDF'.

All three values are already live on prod (set via kubectl on
2026-08-10 by Hung-Fan Lin and Tianhao Wang); this commit syncs the
manifest so a future kubectl apply does not revert them:
- POOL_ACQUIRE_TIMEOUT=30000: queue during bursts instead of failing,
  while keeping acquire+render inside the ingress 60s read timeout.
- replicas 5 -> 8 and BROWSERS_PER_WORKER 2 -> 3: concurrent render
  capacity 10 -> 24. Watch pod memory: the 4Gi limit was sized for 2
  browsers per pod.
- Also sync LOG_LEVEL and CORS_ORIGINS already set live so apply does
  not regress them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 k8s/deployment.yaml | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/k8s/deployment.yaml b/k8s/deployment.yaml
index 513389d..a7b516f 100644
--- a/k8s/deployment.yaml
+++ b/k8s/deployment.yaml
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ metadata:
   labels:
     app: report-pdf-engine
 spec:
-  replicas: 5
+  replicas: 8
   selector:
     matchLabels:
       app: report-pdf-engine
@@ -35,7 +35,20 @@ spec:
             - name: WORKERS
               value: "1"
             - name: BROWSERS_PER_WORKER
-              value: "2"
+              value: "3"
+            # Queue instead of failing during render bursts. Renders occupy a
+            # browser for 2-33s, so a 10s acquire timeout turns any burst
+            # deeper than the pool into user-facing 500s (VP-17651).
+            # 30s keeps worst-case acquire+render inside the ingress 60s
+            # proxy-read-timeout.
+            - name: POOL_ACQUIRE_TIMEOUT
+              value: "30000"
+            # Mirror the env currently set live on the prod deployment so
+            # applying this manifest does not regress it.
+            - name: LOG_LEVEL
+              value: "info"
+            - name: CORS_ORIGINS
+              value: "https://portal.vibrant-wellness.com,https://portal.vibrant-america.com,https://mypatienthubs.com,https://report.vibrant-wellness.com,https://newdesign.report-pdf.pages.dev"
           resources:
             requests:
               cpu: "500m"
-- 
